%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c5970a76594470146bc9ddfa9a763ba0, type: 3}
  m_Name: Virgo Archive
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Blockout.Discovery.VirgoArchive
  Records:
  - Title: 01 / Welcome to Virgo
    Clearance: 0
    Body: 'VIRGO CORPORATION

      Personnel orientation / revised 1995


      Our work began with a government medical research contract in the 1950s. Our mandate: help patients whose bodies reject transplanted tissue.


      Every restored life begins with careful work. Record your observations. Maintain confidentiality. Respect restricted areas.'
  - Title: 02 / Emergency power
    Clearance: 0
    Body: 'FACILITIES NOTICE


      Amber illumination means the facility is operating on reserve power. It is not a total blackout.


      The electrical panel by the entry route requires THREE replacement fuses. Insert each fuse as you find it; do not wait to carry all three. The first restores a local circuit. The third restores normal facility lighting.


      Do not bypass missing fuses. Report damaged equipment to extension 204.'
  - Title: 03 / Carrier maintenance
    Clearance: 0
    Body: 'LINE MONITOR / SERVICE CARD


      The lower maintenance carrier is 96.40 MHz. Tune the workstation receiver, hold a stable signal for two seconds, then decode.


      The carrier carries a repeating service message. A strong signal alone is not confirmation; wait for the lock indicator.


      Please stop leaving the receiver at full volume.'
  - Title: 04 / Staff notices
    Clearance: 0
    Body: 'BREAK ROOM BULLETIN


      Relay Break is approved for meal periods. It is not an electrical training simulator.


      Please return mugs to their owners. Property left in lockers is to remain there until Personnel collects it.


      Night staff: some extensions route to old recorded messages. A ringing line does not establish that the department is occupied.'
  - Title: 05 / Research milestones
    Clearance: 1
    Body: 'ARCHIVE ABSTRACT / MEDICAL DIVISION


      Early studies addressed the rejection of transplanted biological tissue. Later reports describe successful integration across previously incompatible donor and recipient pairs.


      The archive describes a treatment referred to only as the serum. Its production records are absent from this terminal.


      A handwritten note on the scanned cover reads: ''Acceptance is not the same as adaptation.'''
  - Title: 06 / Personnel discrepancy
    Clearance: 1
    Body: 'PERSONNEL RECONCILIATION


      Several station employees are listed as having stopped attending work. Their personal property remains on site.


      The dates on the departure forms do not match the final internal access entries. Each amendment was approved by P. Dutton.


      Status: reconciliation suspended by Director''s Office.'
  - Title: 07 / Dutton private notes
    Clearance: 2
    Body: 'DIRECTOR''S LOCAL COPY


      We learned to replace what was lost. Why did we decide that restoration was the limit?


      The old committees measured success against an ordinary body. Their standard was the flaw.


      Attachment references: observation ward; candidate assessments. The source files are held physically in this office.'
  - Title: 08 / Candidate intake
    Clearance: 2
    Body: 'INTAKE CROSS-REFERENCE


      Radio station applications have been assigned internal assessment numbers. The criteria extend far beyond employment requirements.


      Emergency contacts, unexplained absence risk, and physical observations appear beside interview notes.


      The newest entry is marked NIGHT SHIFT / ARRIVAL CONFIRMED. Photograph retained in the paper file.'
  Extensions:
  - Number: 204
    Department: Maintenance
    Transcript: 'RECORDED SERVICE MESSAGE: Reserve supply active. Replace the three missing panel fuses. Normal lighting returns once all circuits are connected.'
  - Number: 101
    Department: Reception
    Transcript: The desk is unattended. Visitors must remain in reception until collected.
  - Number: 309
    Department: Records
    Transcript: Your request has been logged. Personnel amendments require approval from the Director's Office.
  - Number: 000
    Department: Operator
    Transcript: '[A relay clicks. There is breathing on the line. The connection closes.]'
  HiddenFrequency: 96.4
  DecodedMessage: 'MAINTENANCE / LOWER CIRCUIT

    Three replacement fuses required. Return to the entry electrical panel.

    Voice line: extension 204.'
